<title>BELGIUM: BRUSSELS TRAIN STATIONS BLOCKED DUE BOMB SCARE.</title>
<headline>BRUSSELS TRAIN STATIONS BLOCKED DUE BOMB SCARE.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>All Brussels train stations are blocked because of a bomb scare in the Brussels south station (Midi), Belgian radio said on Tuesday, quoting a railways spokesman.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the railway company confirmed that there had been a bomb threat. An anonymous caller said the bomb was set to go off at 1800 local (1700 GMT).</p>
<p>Train traffic will resume at 1815 if the threat proves false, she said.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
